                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa0f4509-7083-39d1-9503-4adee4496af3",
                        "entry_id": "0a6dc84f-9c28-3807-92b7-d93c5228274c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "female equivalent of неаполита́нец (neapolitánec): Neapolitan (a native or inhabitant of the city of Naples, Italy)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine",
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8179d1b1-ebc4-4c23-be42-40dcb653aab3",
                                "sense_id": "fa0f4509-7083-39d1-9503-4adee4496af3",
                                "text": "Маршру́т был вы́работан господи́ном из Сан-Франци́ско обши́рный. В декабре́ и январе́ он наде́ялся наслажда́ться со́лнцем Ю́жной Ита́лии, па́мятниками дре́вности, таранте́ллой, серена́дами бродя́чих певцо́в и тем, что лю́ди в его́ го́ды чу́вствуют осо́бенно то́нко, — любо́вью моло́деньких неаполита́нок, пусть да́же и не совсе́м бескоры́стной[...]",
                                "translation": "The itinerary planned by the gentleman from San Francisco was an extensive one. In December and January he hoped to enjoy the sun of Southern Italy, the monuments of antiquity, the tarantella, serenades of strolling singers, and another thing for which men of his age have a peculiar relish, the love of young Neopolitan women, conferred—let us admit—not with wholly disinterested motives…",
                                "english": "The itinerary planned by the gentleman from San Francisco was an extensive one. In December and January he hoped to enjoy the sun of Southern Italy, the monuments of antiquity, the tarantella, serenades of strolling singers, and another thing for which men of his age have a peculiar relish, the love of young Neopolitan women, conferred—let us admit—not with wholly disinterested motives…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
